    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 81.88 score against Bello. His matchup is the day's primary catalyst; beyond the favorable SP_xERA of 4.43, he enjoys a massive 14% boost from his platoon advantage and a significant BvP historical edge, making him the centerpiece of our offensive strategy. **Kyle Tucker** (74.46) and **Andy Pages** (67.47) follow closely, both positioned to exploit the middle-of-the-road efficiency of Nelson. While both remain \"Lineup Pending,\" their projected spots in the top half of the order provide a stable floor for both R and RBI, provided the lineup confirmations validate these projections.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the roster required careful concessions, particularly against high-caliber arms. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a stiff challenge against Sale; his score of 55.26 is suppressed by the pitcher\u2019s 2.89 xERA, though his favorable spot in the #3 hole keeps him as a necessary start. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (51.97) faces the daunting Wheeler, where we are conceding some efficiency due to the elite nature of the opposing battery\u2014the catcher\u2019s pop time and Wheeler\u2019s general dominance forced a downward adjustment. The most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Andujar**, who sits at 34.66. While he holds some park factor utility, the combination of facing an elite arm in Wheeler and a negative platoon differential kept him well below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" We are playing for long-term category integrity, meaning we will not sacrifice efficiency for volume when facing arms of this caliber.",
